# clangd configuration.
#
# The sources are C23 (nullptr, constexpr, bool, [[maybe_unused]]). When the
# compiler already defaults to that standard - GCC 15 and newer do - neither
# CMake nor configure has to pass -std=, so compile_commands.json carries no
# standard flag and clangd falls back to its own default (gnu17), reporting
# every C23 construct as an error. Pin the standard here instead.
CompileFlags:
  Add: [-std=gnu23]
